    {
      "id": "201",
      "type": "related_content",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 201,
        "relationship_type": "related",
        "body": "Both ～になる／～くなる and てくる describe changes in state but differ in usage. ～になる／～くなる are used with nouns and adjectives to show something becoming a certain condition. てくる, used with verbs, suggests a gradual change over time. They can also be combined. For example, 面白くなってきた means 'It gradually became interesting.'",
        "first_relatable": {
          "id": 57,
          "slug": "になる-くなる",
          "title": "～になる・～くなる",
          "meaning": "To become (Adjective)",
          "level": "JLPT5",
          "type_pascal": "GrammarPoint",
          "type_snake": "grammar_point"
        },
        "second_relatable": {
          "id": 128,
          "slug": "てくる",
          "title": "てくる ",
          "meaning": "To come to, To become, To continue, To be starting to, Has been ~ing",
          "level": "JLPT4",
          "type_pascal": "GrammarPoint",
          "type_snake": "grammar_point"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "1389",
      "type": "related_content",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 1389,
        "relationship_type": "related",
        "body": "～にする・～くする and ～になる・～くなる express change but differ in focus. ～にする and ～くする imply making something a certain way, e.g. 綺麗にする 'make clean', 甘くする 'make sweet'. ～になる and ～くなる describe something changing on its own, e.g. 綺麗になる 'become clean', 甘くなる 'become sweet'. The difference is between focusing on the agent causing the change, or simply framing it in terms of the thing itself changing.",
        "first_relatable": {
          "id": 728,
          "slug": "にする-くする",
          "title": "～にする・～くする",
          "meaning": "Adjective + する, To make something/someone (more)",
          "level": "JLPT4",
          "type_pascal": "GrammarPoint",
          "type_snake": "grammar_point"
        },
        "second_relatable": {
          "id": 57,
          "slug": "になる-くなる",
          "title": "～になる・～くなる",
          "meaning": "To become (Adjective)",
          "level": "JLPT5",
          "type_pascal": "GrammarPoint",
          "type_snake": "grammar_point"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "1407",
      "type": "related_content",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 1407,
        "relationship_type": "related",
        "body": "化する and ～になる・～くなる both express change. 化する attaches to nouns and means '~ify' or '~ize', e.g. データ化する 'to digitize' (literally, 'to turn into data'). ～になる and ～くなる are more general-purpose ways to express becoming something, e.g. 綺麗になる 'become clean' or 白くなる 'to become white'.",
        "first_relatable": {
